From 148d3bf1c225144f5c695664ba68adafbc36f1e4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Mon, 23 Nov 2026 13:08:43 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(post): the Haas feed word keeps its decimals, so a
 tap feed gives the exact pitch

ff() in haas.cps rounded an mm feed to a whole mm/min and an inch feed
to two in/min decimals. A G84 tap feeds at pitch x rpm, so M1.4 x 0.3 at
S115 (34.5 mm/min) posted F35., a 1.45 percent pitch error.

The F word now keeps three mm/min decimals or four in/min decimals,
trailing zeros trimmed, point always written. A G84 whose written F / S
is more than 0.01 percent off the stream pitch is refused by name.

Refs #3692
Fixes #3694

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
